{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"b093wo2zo","tool_use_id":"toolu_01HNhcLfxv2cRKKajTQhQ7z4","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run3-repo/dc6c8a95-0e0a-448e-a65b-049ff655c2ed/tasks/b093wo2zo.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_4\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of the incumbent `gamblers_run_second_order_side_habit`: people still judge a sequence random to the extent their own second-order, gambler's-fallacy model of a fair coin explains it better than the regular generators they suspect (a switch-biased coin, a biased coin, a repeating short motif with slips, with each person's own suspicion of motifs), the evidence weighed per flip by a fitted power of length, with person-specific sensitivity and side habit. The single change is that people also differ in how often they disengage: on a person-specific share of trials (drawn from a population) a participant does not judge the pair at all and picks a side at random, which caps how consistently that person agrees with the majority even on clear-cut pairs — addressing the critique that people differ in their rate of agreeing with the majority more than graded sensitivity alone produces (a subgroup of near-random responders).\nEOF\necho person_lapse_gamblers_second_order > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'PY'\nsrc=open(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/models/gamblers_run_second_order_side_habit.py\").read()\nD=\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_4\"\nhead='''\"\"\"Person-specific random-guess lapses added to the gambler's second-order chance coin.\n\nRefinement of `gamblers_run_second_order_side_habit` (described below). Single\nchange: each person has their own lapse rate lambda_i (logit-normal population,\nnon-centred, 400 slots); on that share of trials they do not judge the pair and\npick Left or Right with probability 1/2, so\np_left = lambda_i / 2 + (1 - lambda_i) * sigmoid(eta + side_i).\nUnlike a lower sensitivity (which leaves the switch-belief term and side habit\nintact), a lapse caps agreement with the majority on every pair, addressing the\ncritique that per-person agreement rates vary more than the incumbent produces.\n\nDescription of the incumbent:\n'''\nsrc=src.replace('\"\"\"Gambler','\"\"\"Gambler',1)\nbody=src[3:]\nbody=body.replace('''    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\"p_left\", pm.math.sigmoid(eta + side[pid]))''','''    # Person-specific random-guess lapse rate (non-centred logit-normal population).\n    mu_lapse = pm.Normal(\"mu_lapse\", mu=-3.0, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_lapse = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_lapse\", sigma=1.0)\n    z_lapse = pm.Normal(\"z_lapse\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=400)\n    lapse = pm.math.sigmoid(mu_lapse + sigma_lapse * z_lapse)[pid]\n\n    p_judged = pm.math.sigmoid(eta + side[pid])\n    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\"p_left\", 0.5 * lapse + (1.0 - lapse) * p_judged)''')\nassert \"mu_lapse\" in body\nopen(D+\"/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(head+body)\nPY\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"8c813862-08c2-4273-846d-297d9a8dd889","session_id":"dc6c8a95-0e0a-448e-a65b-049ff655c2ed"}
